course: dictionary
lesson: 228
title: Allergic: when the body says no
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: If you are allergic to something, your body reacts badly to it. The thing is harmless to most people, but for someone allergic it can cause sneezing, an itchy rash or swelling. «For a few people a sting causes anaphylaxis, a whole-body allergic reaction.»
explain: Allergic is an adjective, so it describes a person or a reaction. You can be allergic to peanuts, or have an allergic reaction to a sting. Allergy is the noun for the condition, and allergic reaction is the phrase you will see most often.
explain: A severe reaction is an emergency. «Anaphylaxis is a dangerous allergic reaction... you call the emergency number at once.» Never wait to see if it gets better.
explain: Sometimes people use allergic as a joke. Someone might say they are allergic to homework, meaning they strongly dislike it. No body is reacting at all. Read the sentence to see which meaning the writer is using.
fact: Allergic means your body reacts badly to something that is harmless to most people.
fact: An «allergic reaction» can cause sneezing, an itchy rash, or swelling.
fact: «Anaphylaxis» is a severe allergic reaction, and it is an emergency: call for help at once.
fact: People with severe allergies may carry an adrenaline pen (EpiPen), and many schools are nut-free.
fact: Common allergies include peanuts, eggs, milk, pollen, dust, pets and bee stings.
exercise: What does allergic mean? | You strongly like something | You feel very tired after running | You are very cold | *Your body reacts badly to something harmless to most people
exercise: «An itchy rash after a new medicine can be an allergic reaction.» What is one sign of an allergic reaction in that sentence? | A new medicine | *An itchy rash | A patient's record | A doctor
exercise: Jayden says, «I'm allergic to homework, it's so boring.» What does he mean? | He needs an adrenaline pen | His body reacts badly to homework | He has a rash from his homework book | *He strongly dislikes homework, as a joke
test: «Anaphylaxis is a dangerous allergic reaction.» What should you do if someone has one? | Ask them to run around | Wait an hour and see what happens | Give them a cold drink and leave them alone | *Call the emergency number at once
test: In the phrase «allergic reaction», what kind of word is allergic? | A noun | A verb | An adverb | *An adjective
exam: A friend's face swells after a sting and she struggles to breathe. What should you do? | Tell her to try again tomorrow | *Call the emergency number at once and help her use her adrenaline pen if she has one | Give her a sweet drink | Ask her to sit down and wait
